From: HiGoROS-E87N reverse-engineering project
Subject: [PATCH] staging: fbtft: add fb_nv3007 driver for the NewVision NV3007 LCD controller

CANDIDATE / UNVALIDATED. This kernel-source-level patch is applied by the
OpenWrt build system to the vanilla Linux 6.6.94 source tree fetched from
kernel.org at build time (target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.6/), per the
usual OpenWrt convention for patches that touch files outside the
buildroot repository itself.

It has NOT been compiled and has NOT been tested against real NV3007
hardware. See reports/10-fb-nv3007-driver-recovery-plan.md and
reports/11-fb-nv3007-candidate-implementation.md in the HiGoROS-E87N
reverse-engineering project for:
  - the full evidence chain confirming this driver exists (built-in) in
    the original HiGoROS-E87N-1-26-05-09-02 firmware's kernel
    (modules.builtin lists fb_nv3007.ko; the literal strings
    "newvisionu,nv3007" and "fb_nv3007" are present in the decompressed
    kernel Image itself, not just the DTB);
  - the license/provenance review of the register initialization sequence
    (transcribed from lvgl/lvgl, MIT license, which itself credits
    "ArduinoGFX NV3007 driver" — moononournation/Arduino_GFX, BSD
    2-Clause "Adafruit style" license; only the numeric register values
    were carried over, no code structure);
  - explicitly unresolved items, notably: no verified hardware-rotation
    (MIPI MADCTL, cmd 0x36) register mapping — intentionally NOT
    implemented, not guessed.

Kconfig/Makefile diffs below are generated against the real upstream
Linux v6.6 tag content (raw.githubusercontent.com/torvalds/linux/v6.6/
drivers/staging/fbtft/{Kconfig,Makefile}, fetched verbatim, not
paraphrased), verified in an isolated sandbox to apply cleanly and
produce byte-identical results to the intended content before being
folded into this file.

---
 drivers/staging/fbtft/Kconfig    |  6 ++
 drivers/staging/fbtft/Makefile   |  1 +
 drivers/staging/fbtft/fb_nv3007.c | 249 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 256 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/staging/fbtft/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/staging/fbtft/Kconfig
@@ -89,6 +89,12 @@
 	help
 	  Generic Framebuffer support for ILI9486
 
+config FB_TFT_NV3007
+	tristate "FB driver for the NV3007 LCD Controller"
+	depends on FB_TFT
+	help
+	  Generic Framebuffer support for NV3007
+
 config FB_TFT_PCD8544
 	tristate "FB driver for the PCD8544 LCD Controller"
 	depends on FB_TFT

--- a/drivers/staging/fbtft/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/staging/fbtft/Makefile
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_FB_TFT_ILI9341)     += fb_ili9341.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_FB_TFT_ILI9481)     += fb_ili9481.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_FB_TFT_ILI9486)     += fb_ili9486.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_FB_TFT_NV3007)      += fb_nv3007.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_FB_TFT_PCD8544)     += fb_pcd8544.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_FB_TFT_RA8875)      += fb_ra8875.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_FB_TFT_S6D02A1)     += fb_s6d02a1.o

--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/staging/fbtft/fb_nv3007.c
@@ -0,0 +1,249 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+
+/*
+ * FBTFT driver for the NewVision NV3007 LCD Controller
+ *
+ * CANDIDATE / UNVALIDATED — see reports/11-fb-nv3007-candidate-implementation.md
+ * in the HiGoROS-E87N reverse-engineering project for full provenance notes.
+ * This file has NOT been compiled or tested against real hardware.
+ *
+ * Register initialization sequence is transcribed from the register-level
+ * command table in the upstream LVGL project (lvgl/lvgl, MIT licensed),
+ * file src/drivers/display/nv3007/lv_nv3007.c, function lv_nv3007_create().
+ * That file's own header comment attributes the sequence to:
+ *   "init commands based on ArduinoGFX NV3007 driver"
+ * (moononournation/Arduino_GFX, BSD 2-Clause "Adafruit" style license,
+ * file src/display/Arduino_NV3007.cpp / .h).
+ *
+ * Neither upstream project is a Linux kernel fbtft driver; this file is a
+ * new, from-scratch fbtft-framework driver written for this project. Only
+ * the numeric panel register/init values are carried over from those two
+ * permissively-licensed public sources — the driver structure itself follows
+ * the standard Linux staging/fbtft driver pattern (see fb_ili9486.c et al.).
+ *
+ * set_var() / hardware rotation (MIPI MADCTL, cmd 0x36) is intentionally
+ * NOT implemented here: neither of the two public reference sources issues
+ * an explicit MADCTL write for this panel (rotation in the LVGL driver is
+ * handled at the software/framebuffer level, not via a hardware register),
+ * so there is no verified MADCTL bit-mapping to carry over. Hardware
+ * rotation support (if the chip has it) is left as a follow-up item and
+ * must not be guessed — see the report for details.
+ */
+
+#include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/init.h>
+
+#include <video/mipi_display.h>
+#include "fbtft.h"
+
+#define DRVNAME		"fb_nv3007"
+#define WIDTH		142
+#define HEIGHT		428
+
+/*
+ * NV3007 command bytes used directly in this file (the rest of the panel's
+ * command set is vendor-specific tuning registers sent as opaque bytes via
+ * the init sequence below, and are not given symbolic names here since we
+ * do not have a public datasheet-level register map, only the numeric
+ * values transcribed from the LVGL/Arduino_GFX reference — see file header).
+ */
+#define NV3007_SLPOUT	0x11
+#define NV3007_DISPON	0x29
+
+/*
+ * Register initialization sequence.
+ *
+ * Encoding (standard fbtft convention, see fbtft_init_display() in
+ * fbtft-core.c):
+ *   -1                 : start of a register write; the following
+ *                        non-negative bytes are (command, data...) until
+ *                        the next negative marker
+ *   -2, <ms>            : delay <ms> milliseconds
+ *   -3                  : end of sequence
+ *
+ * Transcribed from lv_nv3007_create() in lv_nv3007.c:
+ *   - the leading (0xFF, 0xA5) / trailing (0xFF, 0x00) pairs are the
+ *     vendor "register page unlock/lock" commands that in the LVGL source
+ *     are sent via a separate send_cmd_cb() call bracketing the two
+ *     command lists — reproduced here as ordinary register writes.
+ *   - the delay after NV3007_SLPOUT is transcribed from the LVGL source's
+ *     "LV_LCD_CMD_DELAY_MS, 22" token. In lv_lcd_generic_mipi.c, a delay
+ *     token's count is in units of 10 ms (see
+ *     lv_lcd_generic_mipi_send_cmd_list()), so 22 * 10 = 220 ms is used
+ *     below, NOT 22 ms.
+ */
+static const s16 default_init_sequence[] = {
+	-1, 0xFF, 0xA5,
+
+	-1, 0x9a, 0x08,
+	-1, 0x9b, 0x08,
+	-1, 0x9c, 0xb0,
+	-1, 0x9d, 0x16,
+	-1, 0x9e, 0xc4,
+	-1, 0x8f, 0x55, 0x04,
+	-1, 0x84, 0x90,
